# Datasets and training outputs (kept on Drive); only the dataset manifest is tracked
datasets/*
!datasets/manifest.json
!datasets/README.md
# Downloaded or prepared data inside a plan folder (underwater/dataset/, weather/dataset/, ...); camoedge/dataset.py is a file and is not affected
/*/dataset/*
# Exception: Brackish is CC BY 4.0, which allows sharing with attribution, so its images, labels and LICENSE.md are tracked (see
# underwater/dataset/brackish/LICENSE.md). The dataset.yaml there holds a path of one machine and is generated, so it stays ignored.
# DAWN, VisDrone, COD10K and CAMO do not allow redistribution and must never be added here.
!/underwater/dataset/brackish/
/underwater/dataset/brackish/dataset.yaml
# Ultralytics label caches (labels/train.cache and so on) are rebuilt on every machine and are megabytes in size
*.cache
# Training runs stay local; only runs/weights/ is looked at, and inside it only the final weights excepted below are tracked
runs/*
!runs/weights/
*.pt
*.onnx
*.zip
# Exception (decision D8): the final weights that the training scripts copy to runs/weights/ may be committed for Plan A (Brackish, CC BY 4.0) and
# Plan D (the team's own code, published for non-commercial research only); their terms are in runs/weights/README.md. Plan B (DAWN) and Plan C
# (VisDrone) stay out: their data terms are non-commercial or unconfirmed, which the AGPL-3.0 of Ultralytics-trained weights cannot respect.
# Checkpoints inside run folders (runs/<task>/<run>/weights/) and trial projects (runs/epoch1-check/ and so on) are never committed.
!runs/weights/underwater-*.pt
!runs/weights/camoedge-*.pt

# Ultralytics settings file; it is written into the working folder when the user settings folder is not writable,
# and it holds paths of one machine
/Ultralytics/

# Python bytecode and compiled extensions
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class
*.so
cython_debug/

